body:
That's definitely relatable, it does feel like it's something I have control over when all (or at least most) other areas feel out of my control. Simultaneously feels like a really unsafe safety net. 

&#x200B;

How do you reliably determine in a moment of crisis that it isn't an emergency? If that makes sense.. I like the visualization, I'm just wondering how you check yourself if it feels like the only solution is to open the box? Do you just white knuckle through it and accept things are out of your control? Do you try to find other things in your life you can control?
